Relative Expression of Selected Genes:
Relative expression analysis demonstrated increased expression of several genes in SC/B samples, including:
   •	Junb 
   •	Map2k3 
   •	Mcl1 
   •	Socs3 
   •	Pim1 

Biological Interpretation:
These genes are associated with biological processes that support leukemia cell survival within the CNS.
•	Junb is an immediate early transcription factor involved in cellular adaptation and growth regulation. 
•	Map2k3 activates the p38 MAPK pathway, which participates in stress-response signaling. 
•	Mcl1 is an anti-apoptotic protein that promotes cell survival by preventing programmed cell death. 
•	Socs3 regulates cytokine-mediated JAK/STAT signaling, reflecting altered inflammatory signaling. 
•	Pim1 is a kinase that promotes cell survival and proliferation. 
The original study similarly reported elevated expression of Map2k3, Junb, Mcl1, and Socs3 in SC leukemic cells, supporting the conclusion that CNS leukemic cells activate signaling pathways associated with survival, stress adaptation, and resistance to apoptosis. 


